From a947b9380f45f70bc801d14110953b884d2a7444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:06:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(setup): the setup defines the work offset, not each
 height

A height measured from the work offset no longer names its own slot:
HeightReference::WorkOffset is a unit variant that resolves through
setup::wcs_slot (the setup's pick, else G54) - the same law the post
reads, so an operation cannot disagree with its setup.

- Heights page: no per-height WCS combo; a read-only "Work offset" row
  shows the setup's word and points to the Setups page.
- Project v52: the v51 -> v52 rung lifts per-height slots onto their
  setup when the setup agreed (posting and stamps unchanged), and
  refuses the load by name (WorkOffsetConflict, listing each op and its
  slots) when they disagreed or a setup-less document named a non-G54
  slot. A v52 height carrying a slot is corrupt; the MCP params door
  refuses one too.
- The #196 per-op "height on another slot" post refusal is gone (the
  conflict cannot be built); the one-file shared-word refusal stays.
- Setups page "Auto" reads "G54 (default)"; the setup sheet says
  "program offset: G54 (the default - not picked)"; the viewport plane
  chip names the setup's word.

Decision record: docs/decisions/329-setup-defines-wcs.md.

Fixes #329

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
