From 9369577aeca813c3a44b03ec18059db4bdd78790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:34:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(setup)!: the setup defines the work offset, not each
 height

BREAKING CHANGE: project files are now v52. A height referencing the work offset no longer stores its own G54-G59 slot - the setup defines it. Older builds refuse v52 files, and an older project whose operations used different work-offset slots within one setup is refused at load by name.

Refs #329

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

From 721a41f099a200fee03f5c7b5403451045e2bdf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:03:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(setup): the setup sheet and refusals say the plain
 work offset word

Review of #331 (9369577): the setup sheet still printed '(the default - not
picked)' / '(picked for this setup)', against the rule that a setup's work
offset is shown everywhere as the plain word G54..G59 (an unset setup is
G54). It now prints 'program offset: G58'. A refused offset change says
'work offset not changed' instead of 'not picked'; a test note no longer
says 'Auto'.

Refs #329

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
